        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): harden spooled turn adoption",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where replayed Telegram updates could lose their durable dedupe ownership or be settled by a timeout while turn adoption was still being persisted. That could allow duplicate processing, premature spool completion, or a stalled per-chat replay lane around adoption failures and long-running persistence.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe change makes turn adoption the explicit ownership handoff for Telegram spool and dedupe state. Reply-fence abort authority remains active until durable adoption succeeds, queued admission hooks are awaited, participant timeout settlement is serialized with adoption commit, and polling/webhook claims remain owned until that decision is final. The main-only queue integration also preserves the existing `inFlight` overflow contract while removing canceled sources before survivor retry.\n\nThis forward-ports the release fix lineage from `fa4466009d3e657cd95f11964497d66f6f2e137d`. A leaf spool-record type module breaks the policy/implementation import cycle without changing the existing spool API. The cycle repair is kept as a standalone release backport immediately before the standalone seven-file timeout-serialization commit. No Meta provider work, package metadata, lockfiles, shrinkwraps, generated artifacts, or changelog files are included.\n\nRelease-only lint commit `33b53b5c4365fb57c8275fb2076ce12b0c6862fb` does not need a distinct forward-port: current `main` no longer has its shadowed helper shape, and this branch's replacement already uses the non-shadowing `groupItemsToRestore` parameter.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTelegram replay after restart or transport failure is now durable across the claim-to-adoption window. A timeout cannot release a replay claim while adoption persistence is still in flight, and queued replies retain the same overflow and cancellation behavior as current `main`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `tbx_01kx5wx2fme5phskdbyprzaaq5` (`pearl-shrimp`), hydration run `29089843355`\n- Pre-sync release commit order: cycle repair `ee85c70a560fce7aae49e234a1f4796c58f19bf1`, then seven-file timeout serialization `3df205dfce00fb6ab3093b3ad4017885558e0865`\n- Exact 13-file Telegram/queue/runtime matrix: 846/846 tests passed\n- Full Telegram plugin suite: 139 files, 2520/2520 tests passed\n- Focused queue collect/in-flight suite: 95/95 tests passed\n- Focused webhook/bot creation suite: 151/151 tests passed\n- Focused polling suite: 80/80 tests passed\n- Cycle repair: `pnpm check:architecture` passed with zero runtime or Madge cycles\n- Cycle repair changed gate: extension production/tests tsgo, lint, guards, and runtime cycle check passed\n- Cycle repair affected suite: ingress spool, polling, and webhook 128/128 tests passed\n- `pnpm build`: passed in 89.6s\n- `pnpm check:changed`: all tsgo, core/extension lint, and guard lanes passed before the final queue integration correction; extension lint and the affected queue/Telegram matrices passed afterward\n- Fresh branch structured autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings, patch correct, confidence 0.82\n- Fresh cycle-repair structured autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings, patch correct, confidence 0.86\n- Release branch was not modified\n",
